<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the third</p>
<p>day of four-day English county championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Friday:</p>
<p>At Lord's: Kent beat Middlesex by four runs. Kent 208 and</p>
<p>157 (J.Kallis 5-54). Middlesex 105 and 256 (M.Ramprakash 113 not</p>
<p>out; P.Strang 6-88). Middlesex 4 points, Kent 21.</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: (2nd day) Warwickshire 336 (A.Giles 97,</p>
<p>T.Frost 56; Mushtaq Ahmed 5-66). Somerset 8-0</p>
<p>At Chesterfield: Derbyshire 513-6 declared and 28-0.</p>
<p>Glamorgan 364-8 declared (A.Dale 142 not out).</p>
<p>At Chelmsford:  Worcestershire 394 and 99-5 . Essex 451 (D.</p>
<p>Robinson 148, P.Prichard 120).</p>
<p>At Cheltenham: Durham 86 and 321-7 (J.Lewis 81, D.Boon 66).</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 471-6 declared.</p>
<p>At Southampton: Lancashire 569-8 declared and 103-5.</p>
<p>Hampshire 412-4 declared (M.Keech 101 not out, J.Laney 95,</p>
<p>M.Hayden 94).</p>
<p>At Leiceser: Nottinghamshire 342 and 182 (D.Mullally 5-62).</p>
<p>Leicestershire 267 (D.Maddy 103, N.Johnson 76 not out; C.Tolley</p>
<p>6-61) and 5-0.</p>
<p>At Northampton: Surrey 581-7 declared. Northamptonshire 401</p>
<p>(A.Penberthy 96, R.Warren 72, A.Fordham 72, J.Snape 52) and</p>
<p>48-0.</p>
